# Sketchfab models

When adding or replacing 3D models, **search Sketchfab first** — not generic web image/model sites.

## Search (downloadable only)

Web: https://sketchfab.com/search?features=downloadable&q=Eiffel+Tower&type=models

A linked Sketchfab URL is **not** enough. Confirm `isDownloadable` and a redistributable license.

## License (must ship)

OK: **CC0**, **CC-BY**, **CC-BY-SA**.  
Not OK: Editorial (`ed`), Standard (`st`), NC, store-only, non-downloadable.

If the requested model is Editorial/Standard, search for a downloadable CC stand-in and note the substitution in that model’s `license.json` `notes`.

## Creator preference

1. Search https://sketchfab.com/nazidefenseforceofficial/models
2. Use that creator when a suitable downloadable CC model exists.
3. Otherwise pick the best downloadable CC match (recognizable silhouette, prefer ≲200k tris, no huge terrain/ground plane).

## Wire-up

1. Drop `public/models/{id}/model.glb` + `license.json` and **commit them**.
2. Add the item to `src/data/catalog.ts` (meters + `yawDegrees` so +Z is nose) and tags in `src/data/catalogTags.ts`.
3. Inspect in the viewer at Facing 0°: silhouette cropped, sitting on the ground, scale vs person-male (1.75 m).
4. Run `npm run sync-attributions`.
